- I don't know.

100
00:03:42,067 --> 00:03:43,467
They didn't let us go home.

101
00:03:43,467 --> 00:03:45,600
We spent the night there.

102
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:46,667
[LAUGHTER]

103
00:03:46,667 --> 00:03:48,433
Vince, how was your week?

104
00:03:48,433 --> 00:03:50,167
It's pretty solid.

105
00:03:50,167 --> 00:03:51,600
I'm blessed work-wise.

106
00:03:51,600 --> 00:03:54,700
And the highlight of
my weekend last week

107
00:03:54,733 --> 00:03:57,633
was my friend

108
00:03:57,633 --> 00:04:00,200
who asked me
if I'm down to go on a date.

109
00:04:01,133 --> 00:04:02,700
Blind date?

110
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:07,267
Your friend asked you to go
on a blind date with them?

111
00:04:07,267 --> 00:04:10,100
No, no. They're hooking me up
with another person.

112
00:04:10,100 --> 00:04:11,367
- Ah.
- Introduced you to someone.

113
00:04:11,367 --> 00:04:14,633
Oh, so you went on a blind date?

114
00:04:14,633 --> 00:04:16,400
You went home
without even seeing each other.

115
00:04:16,400 --> 00:04:17,433
No, no.

116
00:04:17,433 --> 00:04:19,367
- It was you, wasn't it?
- [LAUGHTER]

117
00:04:19,367 --> 00:04:21,800
That's why we covered his eyes.

118
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:23,600
You went on a blind date.

119
00:04:23,600 --> 00:04:25,567
- No, no. I didn't.
- You didn't say yes?

120
00:04:25,567 --> 00:04:27,400
It's hasn't been set.

121
00:04:27,400 --> 00:04:30,900
But I'm still hesitating
whether to go or not.

122
00:04:30,933 --> 00:04:33,100
Why? What are the things
you're considering?

123
00:04:33,100 --> 00:04:35,233
Why do you have hesitations?

124
00:04:35,233 --> 00:04:36,567
For one, I'm still a virgin.

125
00:04:36,567 --> 00:04:38,833
- [LAUGHTER]
- [ROMANTIC MUSIC PLAYING]

126
00:04:38,833 --> 00:04:41,267
- [TETAY] It's just a date!
- I'm joking!

127
00:04:41,267 --> 00:04:44,200
You're not going
to do the deed right away!

128
00:04:45,533 --> 00:04:46,733
I'm just joking!

129
00:04:46,733 --> 00:04:48,767
Women aren't easy.

130
00:04:48,767 --> 00:04:51,033
Come on. I'm just joking.

131
00:04:51,033 --> 00:04:52,067
What...

132
00:04:52,067 --> 00:04:54,033
Did you do the deed
right on the first date?

133
00:04:54,033 --> 00:04:56,133
No! I'm not easy, Meme.

134
00:04:56,133 --> 00:04:59,100
I waited three days.
Not right on the first date.

135
00:04:59,100 --> 00:05:01,233
[LAUGHTER]

136
00:05:01,267 --> 00:05:03,533
So you didn't have
any idea at all

137
00:05:03,533 --> 00:05:06,133
or was it a fake blind date?
Or you really don't know who.

138
00:05:06,133 --> 00:05:07,733
No idea at all.

139
00:05:07,733 --> 00:05:11,300
But I guess
I'm having doubts

140
00:05:11,300 --> 00:05:14,667
because I'm not sure if
I'm ready for commitment.

141
00:05:14,667 --> 00:05:18,300
- Ah...
- Because when you start dating,

142
00:05:18,300 --> 00:05:19,533
you have to be ready.

143
00:05:19,533 --> 00:05:22,000
- So...
- But it's just casual dating.

144
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:24,467
But I read somewhere that...

145
00:05:24,467 --> 00:05:28,133
nowadays,
men aren't looking for dates

146
00:05:28,133 --> 00:05:31,467
or aren't
pursuing relationships.

147
00:05:31,467 --> 00:05:35,033
Men nowadays don't date
or enter relationships.

148
00:05:35,067 --> 00:05:40,133
It's not an issue of attraction.

149
00:05:40,133 --> 00:05:41,633
But...

150
00:05:41,633 --> 00:05:44,567
- They want to...
- There are...

151
00:05:44,567 --> 00:05:46,967
There are a lot of
horror stories

152
00:05:46,967 --> 00:05:48,300
about relationships.

153
00:05:48,300 --> 00:05:50,333
Failed relationships.

154
00:05:50,333 --> 00:05:52,833
Toxic relationships.
Things like that.

155
00:05:52,833 --> 00:05:57,700
So men are fine without them.

156
00:05:57,700 --> 00:06:01,667
They're not eager
to get into relationships.

157
00:06:01,667 --> 00:06:04,267
[VINCE] I agree. We prefer
things to happen naturally.

158
00:06:04,267 --> 00:06:05,467
[VICE] Yes.

159
00:06:05,467 --> 00:06:07,500
They just want to have fun.
With or without a relationship.

160
00:06:07,500 --> 00:06:10,467
They don't want to
force anything.

161
00:06:10,500 --> 00:06:13,333
- [TETAY] Okay.
- Aren't you in a relationship?

162
00:06:13,333 --> 00:06:14,800
- Yeah.
- But you're not a straight man.

163
00:06:14,800 --> 00:06:16,433
We're referring to straight men.

164
00:06:16,433 --> 00:06:19,567
But when my partner
was courting me,

165
00:06:19,567 --> 00:06:21,933
I also asked myself,
"Am I ready for this?"

166
00:06:21,933 --> 00:06:23,267
- Because...
- Ah.

167
00:06:23,267 --> 00:06:24,933
- I said--
- But isn't that forbidden?

168
00:06:24,933 --> 00:06:27,733
Isn't it illegal in Saudi Arabia
for men to be courted?

169
00:06:27,733 --> 00:06:29,067
[IN DEEP VOICE] Wow!

170
00:06:29,067 --> 00:06:30,600
[IN NORMAL VOICE]
Because I'm a camel?

171
00:06:30,600 --> 00:06:31,967
[LAUGHING]

172
00:06:31,967 --> 00:06:33,700
- But that's very interesting.
- Mm-hmm.

173
00:06:33,700 --> 00:06:35,267
How was your week?

174
00:06:35,267 --> 00:06:38,600
Oh, it was splendid.
Like, it was perfect.

175
00:06:38,600 --> 00:06:41,367
- The usual stuff.
- [VICE] Splendid, really?

176
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:43,367
Okay, I'll just use Splenda.
[LAUGHS]

177
00:06:43,367 --> 00:06:44,533
- But it was great.
- [VICE] The sweetener?

178
00:06:44,533 --> 00:06:45,500
Isn't that
an artificial sweetener?

179
00:06:45,500 --> 00:06:46,267
Yes!

180
00:06:46,267 --> 00:06:47,600
I spent time with the kids.

181
00:06:47,600 --> 00:06:51,300
I also got to work on
other projects.

182
00:06:51,300 --> 00:06:54,267
We went to my OB-GYN.
I got a checkup.

183
00:06:54,267 --> 00:06:56,067
- OB-GYN?
- Yes.

184
00:06:56,067 --> 00:06:59,533
Yes, my doctor
circumcised me instead.

185
00:06:59,533 --> 00:07:01,867
"This is what you really need!"

186
00:07:01,867 --> 00:07:03,633
"This will get you
to shut up!"

187
00:07:03,633 --> 00:07:07,367
Wow, going to an OB-GYN
is a fantasy for some gay men.

188
00:07:07,367 --> 00:07:09,867
Then my doctor said,
"He's lost it!"

189
00:07:09,867 --> 00:07:11,500
But the doctor still took you in

190
00:07:11,500 --> 00:07:13,033
- to collect the fee.
- Yes.

191
00:07:13,033 --> 00:07:16,000
But what about you?
How was your week?

192
00:07:16,033 --> 00:07:18,467
Well, I had a very loaded week.

193
00:07:18,467 --> 00:07:19,833
- Whoa!
- Wow!

194
00:07:19,833 --> 00:07:21,233
We accomplished a lot.

195
00:07:21,233 --> 00:07:22,267
- That's right!
- Yes!

196
00:07:22,267 --> 00:07:24,533
It's like I had 36 hours a day.

197
00:07:24,533 --> 00:07:26,767
- Yes.
- Like I'm only 26 years old.

198
00:07:26,767 --> 00:07:28,367
I'm very happy I achieved a lot.

199
00:07:28,367 --> 00:07:29,733
I just started filming
a new movie.

200
00:07:29,733 --> 00:07:31,400
- Yes.
- We just started shooting.

201
00:07:31,400 --> 00:07:33,700
Ooh! It's almost MMFF!

202
00:07:33,700 --> 00:07:35,400
We're looking forward
to your movie!

203
00:07:35,400 --> 00:07:36,833
You better be!

204
00:07:36,833 --> 00:07:38,767
If you don't watch it,
I'll make sure you regret it.

205
00:07:38,767 --> 00:07:40,233
Please catch the
Metro Manila Film Festival

206
00:07:40,233 --> 00:07:41,367
on December 25!

207
00:07:41,367 --> 00:07:44,100
It has become our tradition.

208
00:07:44,100 --> 00:07:47,867
And this time, I will be
with Vic "Bossing" Sotto!

209
00:07:47,900 --> 00:07:50,100
[CHEERING, APPLAUSE]

210
00:07:50,100 --> 00:07:51,633
[TETAY] How incredible.

211
00:07:51,633 --> 00:07:53,600
Your schedule is packed with

212
00:07:53,600 --> 00:07:57,133
work, taping,
and everything else

213
00:07:57,133 --> 00:07:59,300
You even have<i>   It's Showtime.
</i>You're so busy.

214
00:07:59,300 --> 00:08:02,500
But how do you maintain
your beauty?

215
00:08:02,500 --> 00:08:05,900
Some people find that
impossible to do.

216
00:08:05,900 --> 00:08:09,867
You make it look effortless!
Do you always feel that way?

217
00:08:09,867 --> 00:08:12,533
Do you feel beautiful every day?

218
00:08:12,533 --> 00:08:14,800
Hmm. I don't know.
Like...

219
00:08:14,800 --> 00:08:17,400
I feel sorry for other people
who need to do so much.

220
00:08:17,400 --> 00:08:19,200
[TETAY] Oh, there she goes!

221
00:08:19,200 --> 00:08:21,267
- [CHUCKLES]
- But I think...

222
00:08:21,300 --> 00:08:24,367
It's the genes and the jeans.

223
00:08:24,367 --> 00:08:26,900
- [LAUGHTER]
- So I'm in denim today.

224
00:08:26,900 --> 00:08:29,533
But seriously,
when you're inspired,

225
00:08:29,533 --> 00:08:31,833
when you love
what you're doing,

226
00:08:31,833 --> 00:08:35,133
when you're excited about
everything you're going to do,

227
00:08:35,133 --> 00:08:36,667
what you do
doesn't feel like work.

228
00:08:36,667 --> 00:08:38,900
It feels like I'm trying
something new every time.

229
00:08:38,900 --> 00:08:40,567
- So it's exciting.
- [TETAY] And you're having fun.

230
00:08:40,567 --> 00:08:43,633
I get to work with a lot
of new people in this film,

231
00:08:43,633 --> 00:08:45,267
which makes me very happy.

232
00:08:45,267 --> 00:08:47,967
Wait, where's my phone?

233
00:08:47,967 --> 00:08:49,200
Oh...

234
00:08:49,200 --> 00:08:52,467
Mister Mel, you still
don't know our SOP?

235
00:08:52,467 --> 00:08:53,800
You know I need my phone.

236
00:08:53,800 --> 00:08:56,833
While I was hosting,
I was wondering where it was.

237
00:08:56,867 --> 00:08:58,267
- I just had it.
- Here it is.

238
00:08:58,267 --> 00:08:59,733
We've been through this before.

239
00:08:59,733 --> 00:09:01,467
If you're short on cash,
let us know.

240
00:09:01,467 --> 00:09:02,900
You don't have to
resort to stealing.

241
00:09:02,900 --> 00:09:05,400
- [TETAY] Have some empathy.
- Come on, Mister Mel.

242
00:09:05,400 --> 00:09:06,867
[TETAY] He's got bills to pay.

243
00:09:06,867 --> 00:09:08,867
- I know.
- [VERNA] Life is hard.

244
00:09:08,867 --> 00:09:11,533
You know, when he was
working on  It's Showtime,

245
00:09:11,533 --> 00:09:14,433
