00:54:21,333 --> 00:54:23,567
- No.
- [AUDIENCE SHOUTING]

1460
00:54:23,567 --> 00:54:25,367
Liars are going to die, Fyang.

1461
00:54:25,367 --> 00:54:28,000
[LAUGHTER]

1462
00:54:28,000 --> 00:54:30,600
- See you got nervous!
- [VERNA LAUGHS]

1463
00:54:31,833 --> 00:54:33,833
He's more of a hugger.

1464
00:54:33,833 --> 00:54:35,000
Ah.

1465
00:54:35,000 --> 00:54:37,533
Physical touch, stuff like that.

1466
00:54:37,533 --> 00:54:40,333
Me too. I like hugging.

1467
00:54:40,333 --> 00:54:41,467
Hugs are something else.

1468
00:54:41,467 --> 00:54:44,967
It's a huge help
for one's mental health.

1469
00:54:45,800 --> 00:54:47,933
You need one hug a day.

1470
00:54:47,933 --> 00:54:49,767
They say it's seven.

1471
00:54:49,767 --> 00:54:51,567
- Why?
- Seven hugs a day.

1472
00:54:51,567 --> 00:54:55,200
Those 20-second hugs
are a big help.

1473
00:54:55,200 --> 00:54:57,833
- [TETAY] You like hugging.
- Yes.

1474
00:54:57,833 --> 00:55:02,467
They say hugs are almost
as good as words of affection.

1475
00:55:02,467 --> 00:55:03,733
Yes, hug me.

1476
00:55:03,767 --> 00:55:05,367
[AUDIENCE CHEERING]

1477
00:55:05,367 --> 00:55:07,300
[TETAY] Hugs are done
with both hands, right?

1478
00:55:07,300 --> 00:55:09,900
Yes, it's 20 seconds.

1479
00:55:09,900 --> 00:55:13,500
Seven hugs a day?
I give more than that.

1480
00:55:14,467 --> 00:55:15,833
Right?

1481
00:55:15,833 --> 00:55:21,400
I'm aware that physical touch is
my top love language to give.

1482
00:55:21,400 --> 00:55:24,500
- Ah, so you're a top.
- [LAUGHTER]

1483
00:55:24,500 --> 00:55:27,167
- [LAUGHING SFX PLAYING]
- No, top to give!

1484
00:55:27,167 --> 00:55:29,233
He has a list, and physical
touch is on top of his list!

1485
00:55:29,233 --> 00:55:31,333
[TETAY] Being on top
is an act of service.

1486
00:55:31,333 --> 00:55:33,867
Hugging is
at the top of his list.

1487
00:55:33,867 --> 00:55:35,200
[VERNA] Next is--

1488
00:55:35,200 --> 00:55:39,000
[LAUGHTER]

1489
00:55:39,033 --> 00:55:40,867
She loves it
when the topic is like that.

1490
00:55:40,867 --> 00:55:42,900
[TETAY]
Yes, she's getting butterflies!

1491
00:55:42,900 --> 00:55:44,567
Do you hug him too?

1492
00:55:45,533 --> 00:55:47,067
Hugging is at the bottom
of my list.

1493
00:55:47,067 --> 00:55:48,800
- [LAUGHTER]
- [SILLY SFX PLAYING]

1494
00:55:48,800 --> 00:55:51,467
- I meant least!
- [TETAY] What is this?!

1495
00:55:51,467 --> 00:55:52,633
Top!

1496
00:55:52,633 --> 00:55:54,900
- Right?
- She's right!

1497
00:55:54,900 --> 00:55:56,167
Hugging isn't at the top
of her list.

1498
00:55:56,167 --> 00:56:00,267
- [FYANG] No. It's the least.
- It's the least.

1499
00:56:00,267 --> 00:56:02,167
[AUDIENCE] He's blushing!
He's blushing!

1500
00:56:02,167 --> 00:56:04,067
- Are you having fun?
- [AUDIENCE LAUGHS]

1501
00:56:04,067 --> 00:56:07,067
- Yes, it's fun.
- It's fun, right?

1502
00:56:07,067 --> 00:56:09,300
Your neck looks a bit red.

1503
00:56:09,300 --> 00:56:10,933
Why? Kiss his neck so--

1504
00:56:10,967 --> 00:56:12,800
[LAUGHTER]

1505
00:56:12,800 --> 00:56:14,000
[TETAY] She's down!

1506
00:56:14,000 --> 00:56:15,333
[SQUEALS]

1507
00:56:16,233 --> 00:56:17,600
- [VICE LAUGHS]
- I'll do it later

1508
00:56:17,600 --> 00:56:19,033
- when there are no cameras.
- Why are you blushing?

1509
00:56:19,033 --> 00:56:20,233
How do you feel?

1510
00:56:20,233 --> 00:56:21,600
Where is that reaction
coming from?

1511
00:56:21,600 --> 00:56:24,233
I don't know... I've always
been like this, Meme.

1512
00:56:24,967 --> 00:56:26,900
He's really shy, isn't he?

1513
00:56:26,900 --> 00:56:29,300
But people who get shy in public

1514
00:56:29,300 --> 00:56:31,800
are the ones
very expressive privately

1515
00:56:31,800 --> 00:56:37,633
to the person
they think is deserving,

1516
00:56:37,633 --> 00:56:39,200
uh...[TONGUE CLICKS]

1517
00:56:40,033 --> 00:56:42,600
of their love and attention.
That's it.

1518
00:56:42,600 --> 00:56:44,833
Who else would like
to ask a question?

1519
00:56:44,867 --> 00:56:47,233
- That girl right there!
- [TETAY] Verna, Vince, pick!

1520
00:56:47,233 --> 00:56:48,267
We have one over here.

1521
00:56:48,267 --> 00:56:50,200
He's blushing because
there's a mackerel there.

1522
00:56:50,200 --> 00:56:51,167
[CHUCKLES]

1523
00:56:51,167 --> 00:56:53,267
Hi, girl. What's your name?

1524
00:56:53,267 --> 00:56:54,267
I'm Myra.

1525
00:56:54,267 --> 00:56:56,667
Myra, what's your question?

1526
00:56:56,667 --> 00:56:59,000
Hi, good evening,
JM. Fyang, and Meme Vice.

1527
00:56:59,000 --> 00:57:00,700
[VICE]
Hello. Why are you in falsetto?

1528
00:57:00,700 --> 00:57:01,667
[LAUGHTER]

1529
00:57:01,667 --> 00:57:03,867
[IN SOFT VOICE] Hi, JM, Fyang...

1530
00:57:03,867 --> 00:57:05,533
My voice really sounds tiny.

1531
00:57:05,533 --> 00:57:08,700
It's okay. Verna's tiny
and she isn't even a voice.

1532
00:57:08,700 --> 00:57:10,033
- What's your question?
- Okay, I have a question

1533
00:57:10,033 --> 00:57:11,233
for the both of them.

1534
00:57:11,233 --> 00:57:12,900
[IN SOFT VOICE] What's your
question for the both of them?

1535
00:57:12,900 --> 00:57:14,567
- [LAUGHTER]
- [VICE] This is amazing.

1536
00:57:14,633 --> 00:57:16,333
Are you friends with Thumbelina?

1537
00:57:16,333 --> 00:57:20,433
Is it true that you fought
when you climbed Mt. Ulap?

1538
00:57:20,467 --> 00:57:23,133
There are some speculations
that you fought.

1539
00:57:23,800 --> 00:57:27,133
- [IN SOFT VOICE] Speculations.
- [LAUGHTER]

1540
00:57:27,133 --> 00:57:29,200
[IN SOFT VOICE] You need
to spit out your phlegm.

1541
00:57:29,200 --> 00:57:31,133
[VERNA] Did you hear
the question right?

1542
00:57:31,133 --> 00:57:32,600
- Yes.
- [VERNA] She has asthma.

1543
00:57:32,600 --> 00:57:34,033
[LAUGHTER]

1544
00:57:34,033 --> 00:57:35,200
What's the question again?

1545
00:57:35,200 --> 00:57:36,633
[IN SOFT VOICE] Is it true
that you fought in Mt. Ulap?

1546
00:57:36,633 --> 00:57:37,867
There are some speculations...

1547
00:57:37,867 --> 00:57:39,300
Oh my god!

1548
00:57:39,300 --> 00:57:43,200
Is it true that you fought
when you climbed Mt. Ulap?

1549
00:57:43,200 --> 00:57:45,500
[IN SOFT VOICE] Is it true that
you had an X-ray the other day?

1550
00:57:45,500 --> 00:57:47,500
- Yes.
- [SILLY SFX PLAYING]

1551
00:57:47,500 --> 00:57:49,967
You fought on Mt. Ulap?
What happened on Mt. Ulap?

1552
00:57:49,967 --> 00:57:51,933
Uh, no. Because it's...
[CHUCKLES]

1553
00:57:51,967 --> 00:57:53,300
[LAUGHTER]

1554
00:57:53,300 --> 00:57:54,500
Okay.

1555
00:57:54,500 --> 00:57:57,067
No, we didn't get
to climb Mt. Ulap

1556
00:57:57,067 --> 00:58:01,333
because it was closed that day
due to a storm.

1557
00:58:01,333 --> 00:58:03,200
But we didn't fight.

1558
00:58:03,200 --> 00:58:04,667
Just a little misunderstanding

1559
00:58:04,667 --> 00:58:06,067
- the night before.
- Why?

1560
00:58:06,067 --> 00:58:08,800
She did something that night.

1561
00:58:08,800 --> 00:58:09,733
What did you do?

1562
00:58:10,733 --> 00:58:12,700
- You say it.
- It's just a small thing.

1563
00:58:12,700 --> 00:58:15,333
I just told her off and...

1564
00:58:15,333 --> 00:58:17,733
Ah, he's like your father.

1565
00:58:17,733 --> 00:58:19,833
I thought you guys
were a love team.

1566
00:58:19,833 --> 00:58:22,033
No, it was--

1567
00:58:22,033 --> 00:58:25,667
I left home around 9PM.

1568
00:58:25,700 --> 00:58:29,700
I told him, "Hey, I'm just
going over to my friend's."

1569
00:58:29,700 --> 00:58:32,633
"Pick me up
and drop me off at home."

1570
00:58:32,633 --> 00:58:33,600
That's it.

1571
00:58:33,600 --> 00:58:35,500
The situation was,

1572
00:58:35,500 --> 00:58:39,333
he waited in the condo's lobby
for a long time.

1573
00:58:39,333 --> 00:58:42,733
He was texting me.
It was around 3 or 4AM.

1574
00:58:43,600 --> 00:58:46,267
He said he's already downstairs.

1575
00:58:46,267 --> 00:58:47,967
Then he kept calling
and I wasn't picking up.

1576
00:58:47,967 --> 00:58:49,067
Why?

1577
00:58:49,067 --> 00:58:50,933
- My friend was opening up.
- And--

1578
00:58:50,933 --> 00:58:52,800
And the guard
was asking me to leave.

1579
00:58:52,800 --> 00:58:56,533
We were already arguing.

1580
00:58:56,533 --> 00:58:58,200
Oh, so that's how you are.

1581
00:58:58,233 --> 00:59:01,433
When you're with your friends
and your boyfriend calls,

1582
00:59:01,433 --> 00:59:02,467
you won't answer.

1583
00:59:02,467 --> 00:59:03,600
Ouch.

1584
00:59:03,600 --> 00:59:06,100
- He's not my boyfriend yet.
- [VICE] What?

1585
00:59:06,100 --> 00:59:07,467
He's not my boyfriend yet.

1586
00:59:07,467 --> 00:59:10,333
Especially if it's your friend.
You asked him to pick you up.

1587
00:59:10,333 --> 00:59:12,633
You still won't answer the call?
But even--

1588
00:59:12,633 --> 00:59:16,067
You'd respond to the deliveries
at your house.

1589
00:59:16,067 --> 00:59:19,467
It's not that I wouldn't answer
at all. I texted him.

1590
00:59:19,467 --> 00:59:23,833
I didn't want him to hear
what my friend was sharing.

1591
00:59:23,833 --> 00:59:26,500
- You texted him, "Hold on..."
- I did.

1592
00:59:26,500 --> 00:59:27,800
She did. You're so dramatic.

1593
00:59:27,800 --> 00:59:31,800
No, she texted me she's
all good and to pick her up.

1594
00:59:31,833 --> 00:59:33,667
So I did. I was nearby.

1595
00:59:33,667 --> 00:59:35,867
Why did you text him that
when you're still talking?

1596
00:59:35,867 --> 00:59:37,767
- It's your fault.
- [CHUCKLES]

1597
00:59:37,767 --> 00:59:39,700
My friend suddenly opened up.

1598
00:59:39,700 --> 00:59:42,800
It was sudden.
You should've asked then.

1599
00:59:42,800 --> 00:59:44,733
Well, that's her friend,
not mine.

1600
00:59:44,733 --> 00:59:47,600
It's not his friend. Why did he
have to suffer in the lobby?

1601
00:59:47,600 --> 00:59:50,233
- You should've explained.
- I said sorry.

1602
00:59:50,233 --> 00:59:52,933
- [VERNA] She did say sorry.
- That was already late

1603
00:59:52,933 --> 00:59:55,233
and our trip
was early in the morning.

1604
00:59:55,233 --> 00:59:58,133
So yeah,
it was just a misunderstanding.

1605
00:59:58,133 --> 01:00:00,133
What don't you like about Fyang?

1606
01:00:00,133 --> 01:00:02,333
- There we go.
- None, I've accepted it all.

1607
01:00:02,333 --> 01:00:04,333
- [CHUCKLES]
- [ALL] Aw!

1608
01:00:04,367 --> 01:00:06,800
None. We've been together
long enough.

1609
01:00:06,800 --> 01:00:08,633
Which of her traits...

1610
01:00:08,633 --> 01:00:14,700
[CROWD CHEERING, LAUGHING]

1611
01:00:14,700 --> 01:00:17,900
Wow, you're acting
as if you even weigh 55kg.

1612
01:00:17,900 --> 01:00:19,900
[LAUGHTER]

1613
01:00:19,900 --> 01:00:23,000
Which of her traits
will make us say,

1614
01:00:23,000 --> 01:00:25,367
"Wow, he accepted that.
That's amazing."?

1615
01:00:25,367 --> 01:00:27,167
What intense trait of hers
is that,

1616
01:00:27,167 --> 01:00:28,967
but because of love,
you accepted it?

1617
01:00:31,333 --> 01:00:33,067
You said
you accepted her wholly.

1618
01:00:34,733 --> 01:00:38,033
I guess she's very,

1619
01:00:38,133 --> 01:00:39,667
uh...

1620
01:00:39,667 --> 01:00:41,567
she's very impulsive.

1621
01:00:41,567 --> 01:00:44,300
When she makes, uh...

1622
01:00:44,300 --> 01:00:46,633
like, a specific decision.

1623
01:00:46,633 --> 01:00:48,633
She didn't think of--
This was before.

1624
01:00:48,633 --> 01:00:50,567
She didn't think through whether
it would be good for her,

1625
01:00:50,567 --> 01:00:52,833
right or wrong.

1626
01:00:53,533 --> 01:00:56,100
It even got to a point

1627
01:00:56,100 --> 01:00:59,000
where her own mom
didn't like her decision.

1628
01:00:59,700 --> 01:01:01,067
Now my mom's in on this.

1629
01:01:01,067 --> 01:01:02,300
- I love you, Mother.
- No.

1630
01:01:02,300 --> 01:01:04,567
Just to emphasize the intensity.

1631
01:01:04,567 --> 01:01:09,333
You've shared that
with Vhong and me.

1632
01:01:09,333 --> 01:01:10,533
He said,

1633
01:01:10,533 --> 01:01:14,233
"Sometimes, Fyang can't control
the burst of her emotions."

1634
01:01:14,267 --> 01:01:15,800
He speaks Tagalog so deeply.

1635
01:01:15,800 --> 01:01:18,500
I remember he's from Quezon.
Yeah, he was like,

1636
01:01:18,500 --> 01:01:21,267
"Sometimes, Fyang can't control
the burst of her emotions.".

1637
01:01:21,267 --> 01:01:23,100
Wow.

1638
01:01:23,167 --> 01:01:27,100
What do you think people have
a hard time accepting about you

1639
01:01:27,100 --> 01:01:28,367
but he did?

1640
01:01:29,367 --> 01:01:30,733
Uh...

1641
01:01:30,733 --> 01:01:32,767
I think being...

1642
01:01:34,400 --> 01:01:35,867
huh?

1643
01:01:35,867 --> 01:01:37,400
- Are you stupid?
- [SILLY SFX PLAYING]

1644
01:01:37,400 --> 01:01:39,033
[LAUGHTER]

1645
01:01:39,033 --> 01:01:40,500
What's the question again?
I'm sorry.

1646
01:01:40,500 --> 01:01:42,033
[LAUGHTER]

1647
01:01:42,033 --> 01:01:45,333
My trait that you've accepted
but others can't.

1648
01:01:45,367 --> 01:01:47,133
But, girl, admit it...

1649
01:01:47,133 --> 01:01:48,733
[LAUGHTER]

1650
01:01:48,733 --> 01:01:50,933
- You get brain farts.
- Yes.

1651
01:01:50,933 --> 01:01:52,733
[LAUGHTER]

1652
01:01:52,733 --> 01:01:55,567
That's it. You've accepted it
but others can't.

1653
01:01:55,567 --> 01:01:57,067
Yes, yes.

1654
01:01:57,067 --> 01:01:59,433
Uh, maybe most of the time,

1655
01:01:59,433 --> 01:02:02,667
from what I've read,
it's the way I talk.

1656
01:02:02,667 --> 01:02:04,900
- Mm-hmm.
- That's it.

1657
01:02:04,900 --> 01:02:06,300
They have a problem
with it so...

1658
01:02:06,300 --> 01:02:09,267
Your true self

1659
01:02:09,267 --> 01:02:11,933
that others don't like,

1660
01:02:11,933 --> 01:02:13,267
but JM accepts it regardless,

1661
01:02:13,267 --> 01:02:15,267
- and loves you even more.
- Yes.

1662
01:02:15,267 --> 01:02:17,000
That's what I liked about her.

1663
01:02:17,000 --> 01:02:23,467
[CROWD CHEERING]

1664
01:02:24,500 --> 01:02:25,933
But, girl, admit it...

1665
01:02:25,933 --> 01:02:27,933
[LAUGHTER]

1666
01:02:29,933 --> 01:02:31,833
That's really what love is.

1667
01:02:31,833 --> 01:02:33,000
That'll make you appreciate

1668
01:02:33,000 --> 01:02:34,267
the people who love you
even more.

1669
01:02:34,267 --> 01:02:36,900
Because a lot of us--
You'll notice it yourself.

1670
01:02:36,900 --> 01:02:40,433
There are things about yourself
that you don't even like.

1671
01:02:40,433 --> 01:02:43,867
But others choose to love
and embrace them.

1672
01:02:43,867 --> 01:02:46,333
And they will make you feel

1673
01:02:46,333 --> 01:02:49,533
that despite having that
or being this,

1674
01:02:49,533 --> 01:02:51,600
it's okay
and you are worthy of love.

1675
01:02:51,633 --> 01:02:52,600
[CROWD CHEERS]

1676
01:02:52,600 --> 01:02:55,300
I will not take that
against you.

1677
01:02:55,300 --> 01:02:57,467
And that will not make you
a lesser person.

1678
01:02:57,467 --> 01:03:00,733
Others choose to use that
against us,

1679
01:03:00,733 --> 01:03:05,433
but some choose to accept
and embrace it.

1680
01:03:05,433 --> 01:03:06,767
It's beautiful.

1681
01:03:06,767 --> 01:03:08,400
- Who else has a question?
- Thank you.

1682
01:03:08,400 --> 01:03:10,767
[VINCE] I have a question here
from Jaylord.

1683
01:03:12,767 --> 01:03:13,900
Jaylord.

1684
01:03:13,900 --> 01:03:15,600
[VICE] How can you tease him
when his name is Jaylord?

1685
01:03:15,600 --> 01:03:17,033
- [FYANG LAUGHS]
- [SILLY SFX PLAYING]

1686
01:03:17,033 --> 01:03:18,167
What's your name, bro--

1687
01:03:18,167 --> 01:03:19,900
[VICE]
You guys kind of look alike.

1688
01:03:20,700 --> 01:03:22,933
- Jaylord really believed it.
- I'll stand next to you.

1689
01:03:22,933 --> 01:03:25,000
Here. Do you see it?

1690
01:03:25,033 --> 01:03:26,233
He's like my twin.

1691
01:03:26,233 --> 01:03:27,533
[VICE]
Yes, you have the same hair.

1692
01:03:27,533 --> 01:03:28,700
What's your question?

1693
01:03:28,700 --> 01:03:30,233
Hi, JM and Fyang.

1694
01:03:30,233 --> 01:03:32,567
- My question-- [CHUCKLES]
- [FYANG] That's not your voice.

1695
01:03:32,567 --> 01:03:34,567
- [LAUGHTER]
- Oh, you know him?

1696
01:03:34,567 --> 01:03:36,067
I know him.

1697
01:03:36,067 --> 01:03:38,033
- Why? What's his real voice?
- [JAYLORD LAUGHS]

1698
01:03:38,033 --> 01:03:39,800
You have the same voice
as the girl in pink?

1699
01:03:39,800 --> 01:03:42,000
- [LAUGHTER]
- No, Meme.

1700
01:03:42,000 --> 01:03:43,400
I heard it now. "No"

